+                 * CAP2.
+                 *
+                 * The confound to kill: that observation came from a warm reload
+                 * with LnkCap2 already 0x6, so "bit3 is masked" and "the trigger
+                 * only fires once per reset" both fit. Sweeping several values
+                 * in one boot separates them -- if LnkCap2 tracks 0x2|v for
+                 * every v except where bit3 is involved, the trigger is live and
+                 * bit3 is masked. If LnkCap2 never moves after the first write,
